#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186229657 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186229143 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3d611c75-818f-508f-a7a4-49edb32baa41" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Homogeneous Initial Value Problem Using a Given Matrix Exponential"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2826f3b3-aa19-5166-9709-c29a10e19d9b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-3\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2t) \\\\ 3\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2t)\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534348} {:answer/id #uuid "4c00ea3b-3ce4-5e0c-8832-b95dc6c0a81b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2t) \\\\ -3\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2t)\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534412} {:answer/id #uuid "5075de84-7cd8-5fc4-90bb-1cd990dbc9ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2t) \\\\ -3\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2t)\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534423} {:answer/id #uuid "70233942-007a-5043-b53a-395ec3709d87" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-3\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2t) \\\\ -3\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2t)\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534501} {:answer/id #uuid "c1df0fbb-0a33-5bd3-9288-292dffd71dcd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2t) \\\\ -3\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2t)\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534698}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "70233942-007a-5043-b53a-395ec3709d87" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-3\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2t) \\\\ -3\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2t)\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534501} :answer-field/id #uuid "ca3c1b24-93bd-5251-bf4f-c0926f7bb2fd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186228132}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4ca0dd99-a2aa-57ba-b99d-effa4b0eacfb" :question/math-academy-id "q-333981" :question/problem "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=2y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=2x(t),\\end{aligned}\\,[\\begin{aligned}x(0) \\\\ y(0)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the initial value problem above.\n\n*Hint: ${e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2t) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2t) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2t)\\end{aligned}],$ where $A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}].$*" :question/worked-solution "Writing our system in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}]x(t),\n$$\n\nwhere $x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}].$ So, the matrix of the system is $A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}].$\n\nGiven the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the solution of the initial value problem can be written as\n\n$$\nx(t)={Φ}_{0}(t)\\,x(0),\n$$\n\nwhere ${Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}$ is the standard fundamental matrix of the system, and $x(0)$ is the initial condition vector.\n\nNow, using the given information, the standard fundamental matrix ${Φ}_{0}(t)$ of the system is given by\n\n$$\n{Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2t) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2t) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2t)\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={e}^{At}\\,x(0) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2t) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2t) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2t)\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2t) \\\\ -3\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2t)\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186311561 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186229143 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3d611c75-818f-508f-a7a4-49edb32baa41" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Homogeneous Initial Value Problem Using a Given Matrix Exponential"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "475bc880-3247-5ccb-b66d-eadc8b060abd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(7t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(7t)\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309293} {:answer/id #uuid "49f14ac6-ae6a-52fb-ac47-59a4da45cbf2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(7t) \\\\ -7\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(7t)\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309314} {:answer/id #uuid "dddc0c7d-92d4-5f6a-896b-0827b4812b12" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(7t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(7t)\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310526} {:answer/id #uuid "e3ce61e9-90fc-5364-9639-0f81ce141cae" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-7\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(7t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(7t)\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310567} {:answer/id #uuid "edf565d5-c17e-5fec-b7c6-a3893ad155fb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(7t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(7t)\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310642}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dddc0c7d-92d4-5f6a-896b-0827b4812b12" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(7t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(7t)\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310526} :answer-field/id #uuid "6a3f0017-0fc8-57f5-b880-e66a5a5ec724" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311073}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0363c023-46f1-587f-a57b-04e2d2812056" :question/math-academy-id "q-335265" :question/problem "$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t) &=7y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t) &=7x(t),\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,\\begin{bmatrix}x(0) \\\\ y(0)\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the initial value problem above.\n\n*Hint: ${e}^{At}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(7t) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(7t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(7t) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(7t)\\end{bmatrix},$ where $A=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 7 \\\\ 7 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.$*" :question/worked-solution "Writing our system in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 7 \\\\ 7 & 0\\end{bmatrix}x(t),\n$$\n\nwhere $x(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{bmatrix}.$ So, the matrix of the system is $A=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 7 \\\\ 7 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\nGiven the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the solution of the initial value problem can be written as\n\n$$\nx(t)={Φ}_{0}(t)\\,x(0),\n$$\n\nwhere ${Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}$ is the standard fundamental matrix of the system, and $x(0)$ is the initial condition vector.\n\nNow, using the given information, the standard fundamental matrix ${Φ}_{0}(t)$ of the system is given by\n\n$$\n{Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(7t) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(7t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(7t) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(7t)\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={e}^{At}\\,x(0) \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(7t) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(7t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(7t) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(7t)\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(7t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(7t)\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186535011 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186229144 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "37e58bb6-6d90-5171-bba2-6ffa5a0c91d9" :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Homogeneous Initial Value Problem Using a Given Matrix Exponential: Shifted Initial Conditions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "68733ae1-b610-5dd9-b95d-12135f00648e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\cos(5(t+2))" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534477}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "68733ae1-b610-5dd9-b95d-12135f00648e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\cos(5(t+2))" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534477} :answer-field/id #uuid "4e339ad0-7370-56ee-a106-ae32b1e3a838" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534876} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4db09dc0-d4c5-5e09-a70f-eae2e3269be4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sin(5(t+2))" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534416}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4db09dc0-d4c5-5e09-a70f-eae2e3269be4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sin(5(t+2))" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534416} :answer-field/id #uuid "b890faf2-939e-5590-92f1-af9dc867356d" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186534938}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "530f8a57-b248-5ddf-8ae9-a8b808f3a729" :question/math-academy-id "q-335435" :question/problem "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=-5y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=5x(t),\\end{aligned}\\,[\\begin{aligned}x(-2) \\\\ y(-2)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the initial value problem above.\n\n*Hint: ${e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t) & -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t)\\end{aligned}],$ where $A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -5 \\\\ 5 & 0\\end{aligned}].$*\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">$[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}]=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"130px\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "Writing our system in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -5 \\\\ 5 & 0\\end{aligned}]x(t),\n$$\n\nwhere $x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}].$ So, the matrix of the system is $A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -5 \\\\ 5 & 0\\end{aligned}].$\n\nGiven the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the general solution of the system can be written as\n\n$$\nx(t)=Φ(t)\\,c,\n$$\n\nwhere $Φ(t)$ is a fundamental matrix of the system, and $c$ is a constant vector.\n\nSo, we can write our general solution as\n\n$$\nx(t)={Φ}_{0}(t)c={e}^{At}\\,c,\n$$\n\nwhere ${Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}$ is the standard fundamental matrix of the system. Substituting $t={t}_{0},$ we have\n\n$$\nx({t}_{0})={e}^{A{t}_{0}}\\,c\n$$\n\nand since ${e}^{At}$ is invertible for all $t,$ we have\n\n$$\nc={e}^{-A{t}_{0}}\\,x({t}_{0}).\n$$\n\nPlugging the above back into our expression for $x(t),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={e}^{At}\\,{e}^{-A{t}_{0}}\\,x({t}_{0}) \\\\  & ={e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}\\,x({t}_{0}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={e}^{A(t+2)}\\,x(-2) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5(t+2)) & -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5(t+2)) \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(5(t+2)) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(5(t+2))\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5(t+2))\\, \\\\ \\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5(t+2))\\,\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186311712 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186229145 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1ff837c0-0ebb-5a9e-acb4-894261e0318c" :knowledge-point/title "Proving the Matrix Exponential Formula for IVP Solution: Homogeneous Systems"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1c34b001-8f8c-572c-b23f-54c9b0c5e906" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "using the initial condition ${Φ}_{0}(0)={I}_{n}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308966} {:answer/id #uuid "2cf1caf8-52d6-5aa2-81ff-73de1341e51f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "evaluating ${Φ}_{0}(t)$ at $t=1$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309083} {:answer/id #uuid "487cf069-3ce8-55d6-8f31-00a5f9dc3430" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "computing $det({Φ}_{0}(0))$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309301} {:answer/id #uuid "8b861976-a2d2-5456-8f84-3e614119c072" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "applying the chain rule to ${Φ}_{0}(0)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309850}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1c34b001-8f8c-572c-b23f-54c9b0c5e906" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "using the initial condition ${Φ}_{0}(0)={I}_{n}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308966} :answer-field/id #uuid "746ca404-3ff2-5606-b348-9000ebf3fa87" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 175921